      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1768817043998,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "System Design: YouTube\n\nRequirement\n\n    - Functional \n        \n        - stream video\n        - upload video\n        - search video according to titles\n        - like and dislike videos\n        - add comments to videos\n        - view thumbnails \n\n    - Non functional \n\n        - High availability \n        - scalability \n        - good performance \n        - reliability \n\nEstimation \n\n    total number of youtube users - 1.5 billion\n    active daily users - 500 million\n    avg length of a video - 5 min\n    size of an avg video before processing/encoding (compression, format changes, and so on): 600 MB\n    size of an avg video after encoding: 30 MB\n    - Storage \n        lets consider 500 hours worth of content is uploaded to you tube in one minute\n        \n        for one min video we need storage = 30 MB / 5 = 6 MB\n    \n        for one 500 hours = 500 * 60 * 6 = 180000 MB storge = 180 GB \n        \n        for a year we need = 24 * 365 * 180 = 94.6 PB\n\n    - Bandwidth\n\n        total bandwidth required = total content (in minutes) uploaded per minute * transmission required for each minute of content \n            = 500 * 60 * 120 = 480 Gbps\n\n    - number of server = total active user / RPS of server = 500 millions / 64000 = 8k\n\nBuilding blocks\n\n    database - to store the metadata of video, thumbnails, comments, and user-related information\n    \n    blob storage - storing all videos on the platform \n    \n    CDN - used to effectively deleiver content to end users, reducing delay and burden on end-servers.\n\n    load balancers\nHigh level design \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n    \n    \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "System Design: YouTube\n\nRequirement\n\n    - Functional \n        \n        - stream video\n        - upload video\n        - search video according to titles\n        - like and dislike videos\n        - add comments to videos\n        - view thumbnails \n\n    - Non functional \n\n        - High availability \n        - scalability \n        - good performance \n        - reliability \n\nEstimation \n\n    total number of youtube users - 1.5 billion\n    active daily users - 500 million\n    avg length of a video - 5 min\n    size of an avg video before processing/encoding (compression, format changes, and so on): 600 MB\n    size of an avg video after encoding: 30 MB\n    - Storage \n        lets consider 500 hours worth of content is uploaded to you tube in one minute\n        \n        for one min video we need storage = 30 MB / 5 = 6 MB\n    \n        for one 500 hours = 500 * 60 * 6 = 180000 MB storge = 180 GB \n        \n        for a year we need = 24 * 365 * 180 = 94.6 PB\n\n    - Bandwidth\n\n        total bandwidth required = total content (in minutes) uploaded per minute * transmission required for each minute of content \n            = 500 * 60 * 120 = 480 Gbps\n\n    - number of server = total active user / RPS of server = 500 millions / 64000 = 8k\n\nBuilding blocks\n\n    database - to store the metadata of video, thumbnails, comments, and user-related information\n    \n    blob storage - storing all videos on the platform \n    \n    CDN - used to effectively deleiver content to end users, reducing delay and burden on end-servers.\n\n    load balancers\nHigh level design \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n    \n    \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
