    {
      "id": "EELS9DlHJQwa6qpPeKA40",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 262,
      "y": 2928,
      "width": 1626.2186279296875,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 616280567,
      "version": 1537,
      "versionNonce": 1166573465,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1768818375727,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "    - uploadVideo(user_id, video_file, category_id, title, description, tags, default_language, privacy_settings)\n    \n    - streamVideo(user_id, video_id, screen_resolution, user_bitrate, device_chipset)\n    \n    - searchVideo(user_id, search_string, length, quality, upload_date)\n    \n    - viewThumbnails(user_id, video_id)\n    \n    - likeDislike(user_id, video_id, like)\n    \n    - commentVideo(user_id, video_id, comment_text)\n\nDetail Design \n\n    - load balancers: to divide a large number of user requests among the web servers, we required load balancers.\n\n    - web servers: web servers take in user requests and respond to them. these can be considered the interface to our api servers \n\n    - application server: application and business logic resides in application servers. They prepare the data needed by the web servers to handle and end users queries\n\n    - user and metadata storge: since we have a large number of users and videos the storage required to hold the metadata of videos and the \ncontent related to users must be stored in different storage clusters. this is because a large amount of not so related data should be decoupled for scalability\n purposes.\n\n    - bigtable: for each video, we will require multiple thumbnails. bigtable is a good choice for storing thumbnails because of its high throughput and \n    scalability for storing key-value data. Bigtable is optimal for storing a large number of data items each below 10 MB. ther fore it is the ideal choise for youtube\n thumbnails\n\n    - upload storage: to store user uploaded videos\n\n    - encoders: to compression and transcoding into various formats\n    \n    - CDN and colocation sites: cdn and colocation sites store popular and moderately popular content that is closer to the user for easy access. \n\n    \n\n        ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "    - uploadVideo(user_id, video_file, category_id, title, description, tags, default_language, privacy_settings)\n    \n    - streamVideo(user_id, video_id, screen_resolution, user_bitrate, device_chipset)\n    \n    - searchVideo(user_id, search_string, length, quality, upload_date)\n    \n    - viewThumbnails(user_id, video_id)\n    \n    - likeDislike(user_id, video_id, like)\n    \n    - commentVideo(user_id, video_id, comment_text)\n\nDetail Design \n\n    - load balancers: to divide a large number of user requests among the web servers, we required load balancers.\n\n    - web servers: web servers take in user requests and respond to them. these can be considered the interface to our api servers \n\n    - application server: application and business logic resides in application servers. They prepare the data needed by the web servers to handle and end users queries\n\n    - user and metadata storge: since we have a large number of users and videos the storage required to hold the metadata of videos and the \ncontent related to users must be stored in different storage clusters. this is because a large amount of not so related data should be decoupled for scalability\n purposes.\n\n    - bigtable: for each video, we will require multiple thumbnails. bigtable is a good choice for storing thumbnails because of its high throughput and \n    scalability for storing key-value data. Bigtable is optimal for storing a large number of data items each below 10 MB. ther fore it is the ideal choise for youtube\n thumbnails\n\n    - upload storage: to store user uploaded videos\n\n    - encoders: to compression and transcoding into various formats\n    \n    - CDN and colocation sites: cdn and colocation sites store popular and moderately popular content that is closer to the user for easy access. \n\n    \n\n        ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
